<html>
<title>How do I play the Studio II cartridge games?</title>
<body>

<h1>How do I play the Studio II cartridge games?</h1>

<p>
The sections below provide brief instructions for all included Studio II cartridge games.
In some cases more detailed instructions can be found in the corresponding game directory.
</p>

<p>
The descriptions below assume you are using a numeric keypad and have selected
<tt>Settings / Use Numeric Keypad</tt>. If this option is not selected, the alternative key
is shown in parentheses.
For Player B, the keys <tt>W</tt>, <tt>A</tt>, <tt>S</tt>, <tt>Z</tt> control direction and <tt>TAB</tt> is used to fire. These keys work both with and without the <tt>Use Numeric Keypad</tt> setting enabled.
</p>

<p>
For MPT-02 cartridges that also run on the Studio II, see the <a href="FaqVictoryCartridges.htm">How do I play the MPT-02 cartridge games?</a> section.
</p>


<h2>Baseball</h2>

<p>
Press <tt>0</tt> to start. Player A bats first and Player B pitches. The pitching player attempts to catch the ball by moving the fielders. Player A and Player B alternate every half inning.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<p><strong>Batting</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
SPACE              swing bat

Player B
--------
Numpad 5 (TAB)     swing bat
</pre>

<p><strong>Pitching</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Up Arrow           inside curve
SPACE              straight pitch
Down Arrow         outside curve

Player B
--------
Numpad 8 (W)       inside curve
Numpad 5 (TAB)     straight pitch
Numpad 2 (Z)       outside curve
</pre>

<p><strong>Moving Fielders</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Up Arrow           move up
Down Arrow         move down

Player B
--------
Numpad 8 (W)       move up
Numpad 2 (Z)       move down
</pre>

<p>
Hold the key down for about a quarter second to throw a change-up (slow ball).
</p>


<h2>Biorhythm</h2>

<p>
Press <tt>0</tt> to start.
</p>

<p>
Enter your birth date using Numpad <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt>
(<tt>P</tt>, <tt>Q</tt>, <tt>W</tt>, <tt>E</tt>, <tt>R</tt>, <tt>T</tt>, <tt>Y</tt>, <tt>U</tt>, <tt>I</tt>, <tt>O</tt>)
in the format <tt>MM DD YYYY</tt>.
</p>

<p>
Then enter the start date in the same format.
</p>

<p>The biorhythm chart shows:</p>

<pre>
P    physical cycle
E    emotional cycle
I    intellectual cycle
</pre>


<h2>Blackjack</h2>

<p>
Press <tt>1</tt> for a one-player game or <tt>2</tt> for a two-player game.
</p>

<p>
For all numerical input, Player A uses keyboard <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> and Player B uses
Numpad <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> (<tt>P</tt>, <tt>Q</tt>, <tt>W</tt>, <tt>E</tt>, <tt>R</tt>, <tt>T</tt>, <tt>Y</tt>, <tt>U</tt>, <tt>I</tt>, <tt>O</tt>).
For a one-player game the controls for Player B are used.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
1                 hit
2                 double
SPACE             stand

Player B
--------
Numpad 1 (Q)      hit
Numpad 2 (W)      double
Numpad 0 (TAB)    stand
</pre>

<p>
When "Cut" appears on the screen press:
</p>

<pre>
1 player game     Numpad 0 (TAB)
2 player game     SPACE or Numpad 0 (TAB)
</pre>

<p>
Each player bets from $1 to $9. Stakes exceeding $200 - $999 break the bank limit.
</p>


<h2>Fun with Numbers</h2>

<p>
Press one of the following keys:
</p>

<pre>
1     Guess the Number (1 player)
2     Guess the Number (2 players)
3     Reverse
</pre>

<p>
For all numerical input, Player A uses keyboard <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> and Player B uses
Numpad <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> (<tt>P</tt>, <tt>Q</tt>, <tt>W</tt>, <tt>E</tt>, <tt>R</tt>, <tt>T</tt>, <tt>Y</tt>, <tt>U</tt>, <tt>I</tt>, <tt>O</tt>).
For a one-player game the controls for Player B are used.
</p>


<h3>Guess the Number</h3>

<p>
Try to guess the three-digit number. After each guess a clue is displayed:
</p>

<pre>
000   none of the digits are correct
001   one digit correct but wrong position
002   one digit correct and correct position or 
      two digits correct but both wrong position
003*  combinations of the above clues (except 000)
004   combinations of the above clues (except 000)
005   combinations of the above clues (except 000)
006   correct number
</pre>

<p>
(*) For example, 003 could represent three digits correct but none in the proper position, or two digits correct with one in the proper position and one in the wrong position.
</p>

<p>
In a two-player game both players enter their secret number before the game starts.
</p>


<h3>Reverse</h3>

<p>
Rearrange the numbers so they appear in sequence from <tt>1</tt>-<tt>9</tt>.
Press Numpad keys <tt>2</tt>-<tt>9</tt> (<tt>W</tt>, <tt>E</tt>, <tt>R</tt>, <tt>T</tt>, <tt>Y</tt>, <tt>U</tt>, <tt>I</tt>, <tt>O</tt>).
The number pressed determines how many digits are reversed.
</p>


<h2>Game Pack</h2>

<p>
This cartridge originates from the Sarnoff Collection at TCNJ (S.572.33, S.572.46).
</p>


<h3>Doodle</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>1</tt> to start. A white dot will appear in the lower left corner.
Move the dot using the Arrow Keys or Numpad <tt>1</tt>-<tt>9</tt>. Pressing two move keys
simultaneously moves diagonally.
</p>

<p>
Press Numpad <tt>5</tt> (<tt>TAB</tt>) to begin drawing. Press <tt>SPACE</tt> or Numpad <tt>0</tt> to erase.
</p>


<h3>Curling</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>2</tt> to start. Press <tt>0</tt> on keypad A or B, depending on whose turn it is.
Hold the key long enough to reach one of the target symbols.
</p>


<h3>Pong Variant</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>5</tt> to start. Press <tt>0</tt> on keypad A or B to move the paddle up.
When the key is released, the paddle returns to the bottom of the screen.
</p>


<h3>Addition</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>6</tt> to start. Add the digits shown and press the correct number.
Faster answers score more points.
</p>


<h3>Freeway</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>7</tt> to start. Press <tt>5</tt> to start the car.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
5     increase speed
4     steer left
6     steer right
</pre>


<h2>Gunfighter / Moonship Battle</h2>

<h3>Gunfighter</h3>

<p>
Press one of the following keys:
</p>

<pre>
1     single-player game
2     two-player game
</pre>

<p>
For a one-player game the controls for Player B are used.
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Up Arrow           move up
Down Arrow         move down
SPACE              fire (tap: fast bullet, hold: two slow bullets)

Player B
--------
Numpad 8 (W)       move up
Numpad 2 (Z)       move down
TAB                fire (tap: fast bullet, hold: two slow bullets)
</pre>


<h3>Moonship Battle</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>3</tt> to start. Each moonship can move in eight directions.
Pressing two move keys simultaneously moves diagonally (for both players).
</p>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Arrow Keys        move ship
SPACE             fire rocket

Player B
--------
Numpad 8 4 6 2    move ship
Numpad 5 (TAB)    fire rocket
</pre>

<p>
Rockets travel in the last direction the ship moved. The player who loses all energy is defeated.
</p>

<h2>Math Fun (TV School House II)</h2>

<p>
Press one of the following keys:
</p>

<pre>
1     Slow (approx. 20 sec) answer speed
2     Fast (approx. 10 sec) answer speed
</pre>

<p>
Next, select one of the following:
</p>

<pre>
1     Addition
2     Subtraction
3     Multiplication
4     Division
5     Combination
</pre>

<p>
For all numerical input, Player A uses keyboard <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> and Player B uses
Numpad <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> (<tt>P</tt>, <tt>Q</tt>, <tt>W</tt>, <tt>E</tt>, <tt>R</tt>, <tt>T</tt>, <tt>Y</tt>, <tt>U</tt>, <tt>I</tt>, <tt>O</tt>).
For a one-player game the controls for Player B are used.
</p>

<p>
When the problem appears on the screen each player attempts to enter the correct answer.
</p>

<p>
For problem type <strong>combination</strong> the game will start directly. For other problem types, select difficulty: 1 (easiest), 2, 3 or 4 (most difficult).
</p>


<h2>School (TV School House I)</h2>

<p>
Press one of the following keys:
</p>

<pre>
1     Slow (approx. 20 sec) answer speed
2     Fast (approx. 10 sec) answer speed
</pre>

<p>
To play this game, you will need a copy of the <strong>quiz</strong> booklet.
</p>

<p>
Decide which quiz you want to play (1-9). The Studio II will show a letter (A-H) next to an empty box. The letter tells you which question to answer. Look at the quiz booklet and try to give the right answer.
</p>

<p>
For all numerical input, Player A uses keyboard <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> and Player B uses
Numpad <tt>0</tt>-<tt>9</tt> (<tt>P</tt>, <tt>Q</tt>, <tt>W</tt>, <tt>E</tt>, <tt>R</tt>, <tt>T</tt>, <tt>Y</tt>, <tt>U</tt>, <tt>I</tt>, <tt>O</tt>).
For a one-player game the controls for Player B are used.
</p>


<h2>Space War</h2>

<h3>Horizontal Intercept</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>1</tt> to start.
</p>

<pre>
SPACE          fire rockets
Left Arrow     steer rocket left
Right Arrow    steer rocket right
</pre>


<h3>Vertical Intercept</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>3</tt> to start.
</p>

<pre>
SPACE             launch left missile
Numpad 5 (TAB)    launch right missile
</pre>

<p>
Holding the key keeps the missile on a straight course.
Releasing the key causes the missile to descend.
</p>


<h2>Speedway / Tag</h2>

<p><strong>Controls</strong></p>

<pre>
Player A
--------
Up Arrow         move up
Down Arrow       move down
Left Arrow       move left
Right Arrow      move right

Player B
--------
Numpad 8 (W)     move up
Numpad 2 (Z)     move down
Numpad 4 (A)     move left
Numpad 6 (S)     move right
</pre>


<h3>Speedway</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>1</tt> to start the nine-lap race.
</p>


<h3>Tag</h3>

<p>
Press <tt>2</tt> to start. The black marker chases the white marker.
Each tag scores 10 points. The game lasts two minutes.
</p>


<h2>Tennis / Squash</h2>

<p>
Press one of the following keys:
</p>

<pre>
1     Squash (1 player)
2     Tennis (2 players)
</pre>


<h3>Squash</h3>

<p>Racquet size</p>

<pre>
Numpad 4 (R)    small
Numpad 5 (T)    medium
Numpad 6 (Y)    large
</pre>

<p>Ball speed and start</p>

<pre>
7   slow
8   normal
9   fast
</pre>

<p>Move paddle</p>

<pre>
Numpad 8 (W)    up
Numpad 2 (Z)    down
</pre>


<h3>Tennis</h3>

<p>Racquet size</p>

<pre>
Player 1
--------
4                 small
5                 medium
6                 large

Player 2
--------
Numpad 4 (R)      small
Numpad 5 (T)      medium
Numpad 6 (Y)      large
</pre>

<p>Ball speed and start</p>

<pre>
7   slow
8   normal
9   fast
</pre>

<p>Move paddles</p>

<pre>
Player 1
--------
Up Arrow          up
Down Arrow        down

Player 2
--------
Numpad 8 (W)      up
Numpad 2 (Z)      down
</pre>


</body>
</html>
